  "details": "Smooth looking is quite difficult with controllers. It has large deadzone for looking left/right while having lot less deadzone for looking up/down. Doing a small circle motion with controller feels more like a rectangle rather than a circle; making diagonal camera movement difficult. This only affect Right Stick, and Left Stick (movement) is fine.\n\nRepro steps:\n\n* Load the game and plug in a controller (in my case, a DualShock 4).\n\n* Push right stick slowly to up/down to get a feel of how it moves.\n\n* Push right stick slowly to left/right to see how different it is compared to up/down.\n\n* Do a small circle motion, you'll observe a rectangle pattern rather than a circle.\n\nI use Steam Input as my controller interface. Steam Input Settings for VRChat - such as sensitivity and deadzone - are on default and they are on equal levels. It works fine on other games and this only happens on VRChat.\n\nBest regards.",
